node.doctext:
The question seems to be, "does perl split the entire string before beginning the for loop?" We can answer that by looking at how much memory it is using.
<code>
use strict;
use warnings;
my $n = 10_000_000;
system "ps -orss $$";
my $x = 'foo' x $n;
system "ps -orss $$";
for my $y (split /f/, $x) {
   system "ps -orss $$";
   last;
}
</code>
The answer seems to be, "yes."
<code>
   RSS
  3712
   RSS
 33028
   RSS
674900
</code>
